        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/k/46a35a/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-08-22T03:45:24.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hello, I am trying to find out if the way that I played Reconfigure earlier was legal or not. I had put out a Swift Bot and a Cryo Bot, Swift Bot was incap and Cryo Bot was still alive. In my Power Up phase, I picked up Swift Bot's card and put down Reconfigure, blowing up Cryo Bot and replacing it with Swift Bot.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I know that I wouldn't have been able to just pick up Swift Bot and put it back down, but how would that apply to a situation like this? Does the restriction on putting a card back down just apply to the card replacing it, or does it last for the whole turn?&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:42:19.356Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 5,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 25.0,
